WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:10.710
Write your code, and press Run. This is a real
compiler, running on your own machine — not on
a server somewhere.

2
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:19.210
Programs that read input get an input pane.
Type what the program should read, then run
it.

3
00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:28.830
The pin remembers your code on this device. It
is off by default, so nothing is kept unless
you ask for it.

4
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:36.050
Reset puts the starter program back, so you
can experiment without losing anything.

5
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:42.570
Fullscreen gives you the whole screen. Press
Escape to come back.

6
00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:52.500
The storage panel shows exactly what is being
held: your code, and the runtime this lab
downloaded so it can work offline.

7
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.000
You can clear your saved code with one button.

8
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:07.070
Or clear the cached runtime as well. It simply
downloads again next time. None of it was ever
on a server.

